Diagnosis: all three remaining failures are *shape* errors, not literal/join errors — the draft executes fine with non-empty rows, so the incumbent's repair gate (error or 0 rows) never fires. sp0362 wants one column but got `*` (the "details ⇒ SELECT *" rule over-fires); sp0755 wants the full joined tuple (`SELECT *`) but got a narrow name list; sp0536 fans out duplicates on a bridge join where the gold keeps one row per entity. The harness has no notion of projection width / fan-out, and the prompt's rules 2 and 6 actively push the wrong way for two of these. Two edits: (a) sharpen the projection + duplicate rules in the prompt, (b) add shape-based repair triggers that use env.execute probes to show the model the actual columns and the duplicate fan-out, spending the second call only when a shape mismatch is detected.

